# Copy to .env (never committed): for login.py, docker compose, and deploy.py's first run. On Lambda, deploy.py keeps
# its own copies in SSM; on a container host, give these to the host as secrets instead.
# From my.telegram.org > API development tools:
API_ID=
API_HASH=
# 32+ random URL-safe characters (deploy.py makes the Lambda's own): python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
AUTH_TOKEN=
# The session: leave unset to read TELEGRAM_SESSION_FILE (data/session.txt, from login.py), or paste it here.
# TELEGRAM_SESSION=
# Your public hostname, once there's HTTPS in front (the default allows only 127.0.0.1 and localhost):
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=telegram.example.com
# Optional. More chat ids, comma-separated, that the server must never read or send to (777000 always is):
# BLOCKED_CHATS=
# SEND_LIMIT_PER_HOUR=20
